[
  {
    "sha": "81df3ace4244a68164aa8ff18081461ab3e28281",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDgxZGYzYWNlNDI0NGE2ODE2NGFhOGZmMTgwODE0NjFhYjNlMjgyODE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T02:53:05Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T02:53:05Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(setup): per-setup post options and the setup's own tool-list export\n\nA setup's post options (skip pauses and homes, one file per operation,\nthread output) follow the document's until the setup's Post page gives\nit its own - the #343 own / follow-the-document law. SetupDef gains\npost_options: Option<PostOptions>, set by the new undoable\nSetSetupPostOptions; the option widgets route to the active setup's own\noptions when it has them, else to the document's SetPostOptions. Each\noperation posts with its own setup's skip switch; the Output and thread\noutput are the active setup's, and a program whose setups disagree on\nthem is refused by name in the verification gate. The setup's options\nsave as an additive SetupDto key (absent = follows), so documents that\nnever set them save and post byte for byte as before.\n\nThe setup's Tool list page gains \"Export tool list…\": the setup's tools\n(T number, name, diameter, kind, holder, operations) as RFC 4180 CSV or\nplain text by the chosen extension, built by app::tool_list_export (a\npure read) and written by the UI without touching the history.\n\nFixes #389\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
