      "message": "Merge upstream/main into issue/389-setup-tool-list-v2\n\nSemantic merge with #155 (program entries) and #388 (one file per\nmount): posted_afters now takes a per-op skip predicate, so each op's\nafter-action - and any Pause/Home entry folding into its gap - follows\nits own setup's \"Skip pauses and homes\"; a leading entry follows the\nfirst posted op's switch. The Output/thread agreement check moves from\nthe retired one-mount clause into the program gate. Pinned by\nsetup_post_options::an_entry_in_a_skipping_setups_gap_is_muted_with_its_op.\n\nRefs #389\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
